       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the FDA-labeled maximum for amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours would prolong any toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the typical starting dose. 2.5 mg is used for frail patients.\n- **Another drug or dose**, if you meant a different medication or a different frequency.\n\nIf you do want 30 mg, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
